= CRANIX Lets Schools Customise Every Translation =

'''Cranix-Solutions introduces customisable translations in the CRANIX  administrators can adapt any text of the interface to their own terminology — either from a simple file on the server or directly in the app — without rebuilding or reinstalling anything.'''

<code>[CITY], [DATE]</code> — Cranix-Solutions today announced the release of '''customisable translations''' in the CRANIX (version <code>[VERSION]</code>). Schools that prefer their own wording, for example "Rechner" instead of "Devices" or "Klassenzimmer" instead of "Rooms", can now change it themselves — for a single installation and for all of its users.

== One interface, many vocabularies ==

Schools are not all alike. A grammar school, a vocational college and a primary school describe the same things with different words: a ''device'' may be a ''computer'', a ''workstation'' or a ''client''; a ''room'' may be a ''classroom'' or a ''lab''. Until now, adapting the CRANIX to this vocabulary meant changing the application itself.

Customisable translations remove that obstacle. Any text used in the app can be replaced, and the remainder keeps the wording delivered with CRANIX. The feature covers every screen — menus, lists, forms, messages — in both English and German.

== Two ways to customise ==

* '''A file on the server''' — A small JSON file, <code>assets/i18n/custom/&lt;lang&gt;.json</code>, holds only the keys that should differ. Anything not listed keeps the delivered text. This file applies to all users of the installation.
* '''An in-app editor''' — Under '''System → Custom translations''', administrators browse and search all texts, enter their own wording and see the result immediately. Changes made here are stored in the browser and can be '''exported''' as a file for the whole installation, or '''imported''' from one.

The two work together seamlessly. The app looks up each text in a clear order:

# the translation delivered with the app,
# the customer-specific file on the server,
# changes made in the app.

So a text only needs to be defined where it should differ.

== Built for everyday use ==

The editor is made for administrators, not developers. Texts are found with a single search field, overridden rows are highlighted, and a filter shows only the customised entries. An export produces a ready-to-deploy file; an import moves an existing customisation — for example from another school — into the app in a few seconds. And because the customisation lives outside the program logic, no rebuild and no new release is required to change a single word.

== Benefits for schools ==

For administrators, the app finally speaks the same language as the school: signs, documentation and training always match the actual interface. For teachers and staff, familiar terms reduce confusion and mistakes. And because the customisation is maintained centrally, everyone sees the same wording.

== Availability ==

Customisable translations are available now in the CRANIX  The editor appears under '''System → Custom translations''' for users with the corresponding system permission; no separate installation is required.

== About Cranix-Solutions ==

Cranix-Solutions develops CRANIX, a comprehensive open platform for the administration of schools and educational institutions — covering users, devices, rooms, software and much more. The CRANIX extends this platform to smartphones and tablets as a Progressive Web App.

